  "manual": {
    "notes": [
      "\"MAYFLOWER\" NOTE CLARIFIED, NOT WRONG (research 2026-07-03): a parent-note on this record's father Richard Ingersoll says \"arrived 1629 Mayflower,\" which reads at first like a claim to the famous 1620 Pilgrim ship (which would be wrong). A period letter (Matthew Craddock, Massachusetts Bay Company, to Gov. John Endecott, 28 May/3 Jun 1629) does list \"Richard Indersall\" among 1629 emigrants, and the 1629 Higginson Fleet to Salem genuinely included a second, separate ship also named Mayflower (distinct from the 1620 vessel). So the note is factually defensible but easily misread as a Pilgrim/Mayflower Compact descent claim — flagging as such rather than correcting."
    ]
  }
